# note       : THIS IS THE PART THE SPATIAL REVIEW MOST NEEDS TO SEE: it is the largest body on the board, it carries the 433 MHz PA, and before this model existed the render showed an empty courtyard exactly where it sits.
# note       : an 18-pin castellated module -- the castellated pad row, the pin-1 corner and the shield can are NOT modelled; only the body envelope is, because only the envelope is what the placement review consumes.
# note       : F.CrtYd measured 39.6 x 21.6 mm, i.e. 0.3 mm clearance ring per side.
# note       : the F33 and the bare LoRa2021 (U3) are selectable variants of one rail (kanban t_1b12a7ab, nested dual footprint) -- both envelopes are modelled so either selection is reviewable.
# note       : TODO(unverified): the 3.2 mm height is TODO(unverified) -- a nominal castellated-module placeholder, NOT a sourced figure; the body is drawn translucent at transparency 0.35 so a render cannot read it as measured
# note       : TODO(unverified): the exact PA/shield stack height and any keep-out above the module
